        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 232.26,
          "end": 236.37,
          "en": "in this ExpenseBucket class in this getter here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 236.37,
          "end": 239.043,
          "en": "where we also had such a for in loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 239.91,
          "end": 241.92,
          "en": "But if you're using it in a widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 241.92,
          "end": 245.31,
          "en": "or in a place where a list of widgets is expected,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 245.31,
          "end": 248.1,
          "en": "you actually have no curly braces thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 248.1,
          "end": 251.37,
          "en": "instead you just have this for in loop like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 251.37,
          "end": 254.34,
          "en": "to loop through a bunch of pieces of data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 254.34,
          "end": 258.06,
          "en": "and then right below this for loop syntax here,",
